div.p:
Kusuga-kan, wooden paddle-steamer; 300 horse-power; length, 243 feet;
                    greatest-breadth, 27 feet; draught, 11 feet; carries 4 bronze guns of 5 inches,
                    2 cast-iron guns-of about the same caliber, and 1 Forbes gun of 7 inches.

Dai-itchi-Teibo-kan or Teibo I, wooden gunboat, screw-steamer, 60 horse-power;
                    length, 132 feet; greatest breadth, 22 feet; draught, 7½; carries one cast-iron
                    gun of 6½ inches; 1 Krupp gun of 5½ inches; and 2 small steel guns.

Dai-in-Teibo-kan or Teibo II, same construction and dimensions as the preceding;
                    carries 2 Armstrong muzzle-loaders of 6½ inches, and 2 small steel Forbes
                    guns.
